Fix alabaster version to be compatible with Sphinx 1.8.6

Alabaster 0.7.14+ requires Sphinx >= 3.4, but the upstream requirements.txt
specifies Sphinx 1.8.6. This causes a build failure during documentation
generation. Downgrade alabaster to 0.7.12 which is compatible with Sphinx 1.8.6.

--- a/docs/requirements.txt
+++ b/docs/requirements.txt
@@ -4,8 +4,8 @@
 #
 #    pip-compile --allow-unsafe --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in
 #
-alabaster==0.7.16 \
-    --hash=sha256:75a8b99c28a5dad50dd7f8ccdd447a121ddb3892da9e53d1ca5cca3106d58d65 \
-    --hash=sha256:b46733c07dce03ae4e150330b975c75737fa60f0a7c591b6c8bf4928a28e2c92
+alabaster==0.7.12 \
+    --hash=sha256:a661d72d58e6ea8a57f7a86e37d86716863ee5e92788398526d58b26a4e4dc02 \
+    --hash=sha256:446438bdcca0e05bd45ea2de1668c1d9b032e1a9154c2c259092d77031ddd359
     # via sphinx
